First, let's find an expression for $\dfrac{d}{dx}[-2f(x)+5g(x)-9]$ in terms of $f'$ and $g'$:

$\begin{align}
&\phantom{=}\dfrac{d}{dx}[-2f(x)+5g(x)-9]
\\\\
&=\dfrac{d}{dx}[-2f(x)]+\dfrac{d}{dx}[5g(x)]-\dfrac{d}{dx}(9)&&\gray{\text{Sum and difference rules}}
\\\\
&=-2f'(x)+5g'(x)-0&&\gray{\text{Constant and constant multiple rules}}
\end{align}$

So we found that $\dfrac{d}{dx}[-2f(x)+5g(x)-9]=-2f'(x)+5g'(x)$.
